# Keep secrets out of image layers.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY app/ app/`, and COPY of a directory includes
# dotfiles — so without this line `app/.env` (Harvest token, OpenAI key, Postgres
# credentials) is written into a layer and stays extractable via `docker history`
# or by untarring the image, regardless of what the running container sets.
#
# It is also pointless: docker-compose supplies the same file at runtime through
# `env_file`, so the baked copy is never the one being read.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Build context hygiene — none of this belongs in the image, and excluding it
# makes builds faster and layers smaller.
.git
.gitignore
.venv
venv
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
node_modules
**/node_modules
ui
infra
.github
.claude
.agent
docs
supabase
tests
*.md
!README.md
